Hook Operations:
    allows you to execute custom Operations at select points 
    during linking sources and managing virtual

    For example, you may want to prevent your monitoring systems from triggering during VDB startup and shutdown. In this case, you would leverage pre- and post-hooks to run required scripts for VDB start/stop operations.

dsource hooks:
    Pre sync: operations are executed before a SnapSync of a dSource.

    Post Sync: operations are executed after a SnapSync operation of a dSource.

VDB Hooks:
    Configure Clone: 
        Operation performed after intial provisioning and after a refresh

    Pre Refresh: 
        Operations performed before a refresh.
        These operations can export or backup data from the Virtual dataset , so that it can be restored after the refresh completes.

    Post Refresh:
        Operations performed after a refresh
        after virtual dataset started and configure clone hook
        This hook will not run if the refresh or Pre Refresh hook operations fails
    
    Pre Rollback:
        Operations performed before a rollback, also known as rewind.

        These operations can export or backup data from the virtual dataset to be restored after the rewind (rollback) completes.

    Post Rollback:
        Operations performed after a rollback, also known as rewind
        This hook will not run if the rewind or Pre Rewind hook operations fail.

    Pre Snapshot:
        Operations performed before a snapshot.

    Post snapshot:
        Operations performed after a snapshot.
        This hook will run regardless of the success of the snapshot or Pre Snapshot hook operations.

    Pre start:
        Operations performed before the startup of a VDB or vFile.
    
    Post Start:
        Operations performed after the startup of a VDB or vFile.

        These operation allows us to clean up any temporary files or restart processes that may have been stopped by pre start hook or log notification

    Pre stop:
        Operations performed before the shutdown of a VDB or vFile.

    Post Stop:
        Operations performed after the shutdown of a VDB or vFile.

        These operations can be used to log notifications, clean up any temporary files, or manage related processes.
    
Staging Server Hooks:
    Staging Server hooks are currently applicable to SAP ASE and staged plugins (Db2, HANA, and PostgreSQL) environments, and execute on the configured staging server.

    Pre Validated Sync: Operations performed on a staging server before validated sync.

    Post Validated Sync: Operations performed on a staging server before validating sync

    To edit Hook operations on a dataset, navigate to the Datasets page and select the dataset you would like to edit from the left hand menu. Click on the Configuration tab and then the Hooks Tab. 

    To easily manage hooks across multiple datasets, you can create Hook Templates to apply the same hook to many objects. 

    Exporting a hook template:
        * In the Datasets panel, select a dataset.
        * Click the Configuration tab.
        * Within the Configuration tab, click the Hooks tab.
        * Select the hook to edit.
        * Click the Plus icon to add a new operation.
        * Select the type of operation.
        * Click the text area and edit the contents of the operation.
        * Click Export.
        * Enter a Name for the template.
        * Enter a Description detailing what the operation does or how to use it.
        Click Export.

